WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.967
Every long campaign eventually becomes a split screen. One player is half a city away. One sheet is stale.

2
00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:17.933
The GM has too many windows open and no patience left for false confidence.

3
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:26.900
The epic version of NEXUS-PAN begins there, with trust as the first dramatic question. Who is connected. What changed.

4
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:35.867
Which state is current enough to act on without breaking the scene. Packets move. Devices disagree.

5
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:44.833
The table does not need more drama from the software. It needs signal. It needs context.

6
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:53.800
It needs a clear next step before momentum dies.

7
00:00:53.800 --> 00:01:02.767
When conflict appears, the system should expose it cleanly and let the GM make the call before the fiction tears.

8
00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:11.733
The campaign should travel with the crew from desk to tablet to train to home table without export rituals, copied files, or wishful thinking.

9
00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:20.700
The returning player should receive the humane version of continuity: where you were, what changed, and what move is waiting.

10
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:29.667
That is the fantasy here. Less ceremony. Less panic. More run.
